 Not because of anything we do,

521
00:30:15,980 --> 00:30:18,740
 but only because of what he has done for us.

522
00:30:18,740 --> 00:30:22,860
 So I'll go back, I had that picture of my wife,

523
00:30:22,860 --> 00:30:24,580
 so I'm gonna flip the analogy a little bit,

524
00:30:24,580 --> 00:30:27,860
 but when we got married, she's a year older than me,

525
00:30:27,860 --> 00:30:30,900
 and so she had graduated college,

526
00:30:30,900 --> 00:30:33,220
 gotten a job as a teacher,

527
00:30:33,220 --> 00:30:35,500
 and I was still in college,

528
00:30:35,500 --> 00:30:39,020
 which meant for that year before we got married,

529
00:30:39,020 --> 00:30:44,020
 she had cash flow and I had no cash flow.

530
00:30:44,020 --> 00:30:50,220
 She ate normal food, I ate ramen noodles, most meals.

531
00:30:51,460 --> 00:30:55,500
 So that was the year before we got married

532
00:30:55,500 --> 00:31:00,500
 and then we stood in front of a church building one day,

533
00:31:00,500 --> 00:31:02,620
 we united our lives together,

534
00:31:02,620 --> 00:31:05,940
 and on that day, I received so many amazing things,

535
00:31:05,940 --> 00:31:10,260
 most importantly, being a beautiful, Jesus-loving wife.

536
00:31:10,260 --> 00:31:13,900
 But do you know what else I received on that day?

537
00:31:13,900 --> 00:31:16,860
 Cash flow.

538
00:31:16,860 --> 00:31:19,660
 It was great.

539
00:31:21,300 --> 00:31:24,260
 Standing there, I had nothing in my bank account.

540
00:31:24,260 --> 00:31:26,780
 I said two words, "I do."

541
00:31:26,780 --> 00:31:28,020
 She said the same.

542
00:31:28,020 --> 00:31:31,860
 At that moment, everything that belonged to her

543
00:31:31,860 --> 00:31:33,020
 became mine.

544
00:31:33,020 --> 00:31:36,620
 I didn't have to go teach her class,

545
00:31:36,620 --> 00:31:40,460
 I didn't have to go wipe their snotty noses,

546
00:31:40,460 --> 00:31:41,580
 I didn't have to do anything.

547
00:31:41,580 --> 00:31:44,820
 Simply by the fact that my life was united with hers,

548
00:31:44,820 --> 00:31:49,160
 everything that belonged to her now belonged to me.

549
00:31:49,160 --> 00:31:52,360
 This is the miracle of salvation.

550
00:31:52,360 --> 00:31:55,140
 You unite your life with Jesus.

551
00:31:55,140 --> 00:31:57,020
 You don't have to do a thing.

552
00:31:57,020 --> 00:32:00,220
 Simply by the fact that your life is united with his,

553
00:32:00,220 --> 00:32:04,500
 everything that belongs to him becomes yours.

554
00:32:04,500 --> 00:32:07,620
 Righteousness, you're counted righteous.

555
00:32:07,620 --> 00:32:11,540
 Holiness, wisdom, redemption, strength,

556
00:32:11,540 --> 00:32:14,980
 peace, hope, joy, meaning, life,

557
00:32:14,980 --> 00:32:18,940
 it goes on and on and on just because you're in Jesus

558
00:32:18,940 --> 00:32:20,220
 and he's in you.

559
00:32:20,220 --> 00:32:21,540
 Bring out the tubs.

560
00:32:21,540 --> 00:32:26,420
 So, all that leads to the next true characteristic

561
00:32:26,420 --> 00:32:27,860
 of God's invitation.

562
00:32:27,860 --> 00:32:30,740
 It is fulfilling and it's freeing.

563
00:32:30,740 --> 00:32:34,120
 So fulfilling and freeing, two.

564
00:32:34,120 --> 00:32:35,100
 Get the imagery.

565
00:32:35,100 --> 00:32:38,740
 It's water for the thirsty.

566
00:32:38,740 --> 00:32:41,500
 It's food for the hungry.

567
00:32:41,500 --> 00:32:46,500
 It's all the wine and milk you could want.

568
00:32:46,500 --> 00:32:50,180
 Delight yourself in rich food,

569
00:32:50,180 --> 00:32:53,060
 which all begs the question, what's the water?

570
00:32:53,060 --> 00:32:53,900
 What's the wine?

571
00:32:53,900 --> 00:32:54,720
 What's the milk?

572
00:32:54,720 --> 00:32:55,820
 What's this rich food?

573
00:32:55,820 --> 00:33:00,620
 Verse three, incline your ear and come to me.

574
00:33:00,620 --> 00:33:03,300
 He's it.

575
00:33:03,300 --> 00:33:09,500
 God is the only one who can ultimately fulfill

576
00:33:09,500 --> 00:33:14,780
 all the desires of your soul.

577
00:33:16,280 --> 00:33:18,420
 So, brothers and sisters in Christ,

578
00:33:18,420 --> 00:33:21,460
 God fulfills the deepest desires of your soul,

579
00:33:21,460 --> 00:33:24,440
 which means you are free to stop living

580
00:33:24,440 --> 00:33:26,500
 for the idols of this world.

581
00:33:26,500 --> 00:33:29,120
 Stop gathering for worship on Sunday,

582
00:33:29,120 --> 00:33:30,820
 then turning the rest of the week

583
00:33:30,820 --> 00:33:34,780
 to bow at the idolatry of work and achievement

584
00:33:34,780 --> 00:33:37,780
 and approval and appearance and body image

585
00:33:37,780 --> 00:33:41,820
 and control and comfort and money and possessions

586
00:33:41,820 --> 00:33:46,420
 and sex and pornography and success and sports.

587
00:33:46,420 --> 00:33:49,500
 Check your hearts if 11 college students

588
00:33:49,500 --> 00:33:51,380
 running around on a field on a Saturday

589
00:33:51,380 --> 00:33:54,420
 with a pigskin in their hands captures your attention

590
00:33:54,420 --> 00:33:56,740
 and ignites your affections more than God.

591
00:33:56,740 --> 00:33:58,420
 You have the wrong God.

592
00:33:58,420 --> 00:34:01,860
 Whatever good gift in this world

593
00:34:01,860 --> 00:34:04,740
 that you are tempted to treat as God,

594
00:34:04,740 --> 00:34:06,260
 hear his voice.

595
00:34:06,260 --> 00:34:10,500
 Why would you spend your money for that which isn't bread

596
00:34:10,500 --> 00:34:14,340
 and your labor for that which does not satisfy,

597
00:34:14,340 --> 00:34:17,680
 does not compare to the God who made you?

598
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:20,020
 Lift your eyes.

599
00:34:20,020 --> 00:34:22,780
 C.S. Lewis said, "We're half-hearted creatures

600
00:34:22,780 --> 00:34:25,320
 "fooling about with drink and sex and ambition

601
00:34:25,320 --> 00:34:28,160
 "when infinite joy has been offered us,

602
00:34:28,160 --> 00:34:30,740
 "like ignorant children who go on making mud pies

603
00:34:30,740 --> 00:34:32,760
 "in the slum because we cannot imagine

604
00:34:32,760 --> 00:34:35,260
 "what is meant by the offer of a holiday at the sea."

605
00:34:35,260 --> 00:34:37,740
 He says, "We are far too easily pleased."

606
00:34:37,740 --> 00:34:40,540
 If this world, it's what's satisfying you,

607
00:34:40,540 --> 00:34:42,660
 it's not because your desires are too strong,

608
00:34:42,660 --> 00:34:44,860
 it's because your desires are too weak.

609
00:34:44,860 --> 00:34:47,580
 It takes so little to satisfy you

610
00:34:47,580 --> 00:34:50,380
 when you've been offered infinite joy,

611
00:34:50,380 --> 00:34:52,700
 infinite hope, infinite peace,

612
00:34:52,700 --> 00:34:54,920
 infinite strength, and infinite life.

613
00:34:54,920 --> 00:34:57,900
 Fulfilling and freeing.

614
00:34:57,900 --> 00:35:01,660
 So how do you leave behind these idols?

615
00:35:01,660 --> 00:35:03,500
 That's the next characteristic of God's invitation.

616
00:35:03,500 --> 00:35:04,780
 It's cleansing.

617
00:35:04,780 --> 00:35:08,080
 Verse seven, "So let the wicked forsake his way.

618
00:35:08,080 --> 00:35:10,360
 "Let the unrighteous man forsake his thoughts.

619
00:35:10,360 --> 00:35:12,760
 "Let him return to the Lord."

620
00:35:12,760 --> 00:35:16,980
 Who needs to return to the Lord as your one thing today?

621
00:35:16,980 --> 00:35:23,000
 Who needs to turn away from unrighteous thoughts?

622
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:27,900
 Who needs to confess wicked ways,

623
00:35:27,900 --> 00:35:31,620
 wicked words, wicked motives, wicked desires?

624
00:35:32,700 --> 00:35:35,020
 If we are not careful, we can come into this gathering,

625
00:35:35,020 --> 00:35:37,980
 go through motions, sing some songs, hear a sermon,

626
00:35:37,980 --> 00:35:40,900
 walk out holding onto the same sin we came in here with.

627
00:35:40,900 --> 00:35:42,080
 Don't do it.

628
00:35:42,080 --> 00:35:47,020
 Seek the Lord in confession of sin.

629
00:35:47,020 --> 00:35:51,740
 That verse seven, "So that he may have compassion on him.

630
00:35:51,740 --> 00:35:55,300
 "To our God, for he will abundantly pardon."

631
00:35:55,300 --> 00:35:56,920
 Next characteristic of God's invitation,

632
00:35:56,920 --> 00:35:59,080
 it is compassionate.

633
00:35:59,080 --> 00:36:02,660
 There is so much compassion in God.

634
00:36:02,660 --> 00:36:03,900
 He doesn't just pardon.

635
00:36:03,900 --> 00:36:08,460
 He abundantly pardons all our sins.

636
00:36:08,460 --> 00:36:10,880
 This is the mercy that's pursuing you

637
00:36:10,880 --> 00:36:12,300
 right now in this moment,

638
00:36:12,300 --> 00:36:14,000
 which is why verse six says,

639
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:16,160
 "Seek the Lord while he may be found.

640
00:36:16,160 --> 00:36:18,360
 "Call upon him while he is near."

641
00:36:18,360 --> 00:36:23,040
 So next characteristic, God's invitation is urgent.

642
00:36:23,040 --> 00:36:23,920
 It's urgent.

643
00:36:23,920 --> 00:36:26,320
 Don't miss what this verse is saying.

644
00:36:26,320 --> 00:36:27,160
 In the second service,

645
00:36:27,160 --> 00:36:28,460
 we're gonna take this to a whole other level,

646
00:36:28,460 --> 00:36:31,240
 but for now, in this moment, just let it soak in.

647
00:36:31,240 --> 00:36:35,800
 God is near to sinners.

648
00:36:35,800 --> 00:36:40,220
 He's near to us right now,

649
00:36:40,220 --> 00:36:47,040
 and he will be found by sinners who seek him.

650
00:36:47,040 --> 00:36:53,400
 Yet the implication is clear,

651
00:36:53,400 --> 00:36:57,180
 that there's coming a day when he will not be found,

652
00:36:57,180 --> 00:37:00,320
 and he will not be near.

653
00:37:01,960 --> 00:37:04,800
 And the message of the Bible is crystal clear on this.

654
00:37:04,800 --> 00:37:09,080
 All who confess their sin and trust in Jesus

655
00:37:09,080 --> 00:37:11,120
 as Savior and Lord of their lives

656
00:37:11,120 --> 00:37:13,520
 will have eternal life with God,

657
00:37:13,520 --> 00:37:19,240
 and all who continue in sin with no trust in Jesus

658
00:37:19,240 --> 00:37:21,480
 as Savior and Lord of their lives

659
00:37:21,480 --> 00:37:25,240
 will experience eternal judgment from God,

660
00:37:27,960 --> 00:37:32,400
 which Jesus himself describes as a hell full of agonizing

661
00:37:32,400 --> 00:37:35,300
 fire that will never, ever end.

662
00:37:35,300 --> 00:37:39,880
 At which point people ask, is that literal?

663
00:37:39,880 --> 00:37:43,920
 I mean, does Jesus mean hell is literally a place of fire,

664
00:37:43,920 --> 00:37:46,100
 or is that just symbolic language?

665
00:37:46,100 --> 00:37:47,320
 To which I respond,

666
00:37:47,320 --> 00:37:53,000
 what's the comfort if it's symbolic?

667
00:37:53,000 --> 00:37:57,780
 Like a point of a symbol is to express in words

668
00:37:57,780 --> 00:37:59,720
 that which can't be expressed in words.

669
00:37:59,720 --> 00:38:04,280
 If fiery hell is a symbol,

670
00:38:04,280 --> 00:38:06,760
 what's it a symbol for, a winter retreat?

671
00:38:06,760 --> 00:38:11,400
 It's a symbol for something worse

672
00:38:11,400 --> 00:38:12,760
 than could be put in words.

673
00:38:12,760 --> 00:38:16,120
 This is Jesus speaking, warning us.

674
00:38:16,120 --> 00:38:20,320
 God is saying to a room full of people today

675
00:38:20,320 --> 00:38:26,000
 who are not guaranteed another breath in this world,

676
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:29,080
 enjoy my love right now.

677
00:38:29,080 --> 00:38:33,200
 I'm here, I'm near to you.

678
00:38:33,200 --> 00:38:34,760
 Don't wait 'til tomorrow.

679
00:38:34,760 --> 00:38:36,280
 You're not guaranteed tomorrow.

680
00:38:36,280 --> 00:38:38,200
 I'm near to you now.

681
00:38:38,200 --> 00:38:44,840
 And for Christians who are holding onto, hiding sin,

682
00:38:44,840 --> 00:38:50,080
 trying to gloss over sin, who do you think you're fooling?

683
00:38:50,080 --> 00:38:55,520
 You're fooling yourself, and you're living as a slave

684
00:38:55,520 --> 00:38:59,520
 when you've been called to live as a son of God,

685
00:38:59,520 --> 00:39:03,840
 a daughter of God in the freedom he gives.

686
00:39:03,840 --> 00:39:08,360
 Why continue in slavery another moment?

687
00:39:08,360 --> 00:39:12,560
 Be free in Christ.

688
00:39:12,560 --> 00:39:18,800
 He is near to sinners, and he is near to sufferers.

689
00:39:18,800 --> 00:39:21,920
 I am confident that in a room this size,

690
00:39:21,920 --> 00:39:24,620
 many of you are hurting right now.

691
00:39:24,620 --> 00:39:27,560
 Many of you are tired, you're discouraged,

692
00:39:27,560 --> 00:39:29,760
 you're worried, you're anxious,

693
00:39:29,760 --> 00:39:33,360
 you're afraid, brokenhearted.

694
00:39:33,360 --> 00:39:35,360
 And there is an urgency in this invitation

695
00:39:35,360 --> 00:39:38,440
 to sinners as well as sufferers.

696
00:39:38,440 --> 00:39:41,920
 God is saying right now, I am near to you.

697
00:39:41,920 --> 00:39:45,280
 Do not spend another moment trying to carry this

698
00:39:45,280 --> 00:39:46,260
 on your own.

699
00:39:46,260 --> 00:39:49,360
 Cast your cares on me.

700
00:39:49,360 --> 00:39:51,320
 I will care for you.

701
00:39:51,320 --> 00:39:55,920
 I will care, all come to me, all who are weary

702
00:39:55,920 --> 00:40:00,260
 and heavy laden, and I will give you rest now.

703
00:40:00,260 --> 00:40:05,080
 Even to go back to the imagery of the husband,

704
00:40:05,080 --> 00:40:07,800
 some of you have been hurt by people close to you

705
00:40:07,800 --> 00:40:10,560
 in such a way that you're hesitant to trust in anyone.

706
00:40:10,560 --> 00:40:13,760
 I simply want you to hear God saying to all of you

707
00:40:13,760 --> 00:40:15,920
 who are in Christ, God's saying,

708
00:40:15,920 --> 00:40:20,080
 I will always, always, always be faithful to you.

709
00:40:20,080 --> 00:40:23,240
 And I will never, ever, ever fail you.

710
00:40:23,240 --> 00:40:26,520
 Which leads to the last characteristic

711
00:40:26,520 --> 00:40:28,600
 of this invitation from God

712
00:40:28,600 --> 00:40:31,360
 that's going to lead us into a time to respond.

713
00:40:31,360 --> 00:40:32,980
 It is humbling.

714
00:40:32,980 --> 00:40:34,920
 It's humbling.

715
00:40:34,920 --> 00:40:39,460
 Meaning there's no way to respond to this invitation

716
00:40:39,460 --> 00:40:42,520
 with pride in our hearts.

717
00:40:42,520 --> 00:40:46,640
 Psalm 95 gives us instructions for how to respond

718
00:40:46,640 --> 00:40:49,080
 to this invitation using same language

719
00:40:49,080 --> 00:40:51,320
 as Isaiah 54 and five.

720
00:40:51,320 --> 00:40:55,780
 O come, let us worship and bow down.

721
00:40:55,780 --> 00:40:59,040
 Let us kneel before the Lord, our maker,

722
00:40:59,040 --> 00:41:00,840
 for he is our God.

723
00:41:00,840 --> 00:41:04,780
 We are the people of his pasture and the sheep of his hand.

724
00:41:04,780 --> 00:41:09,780
 Bowing down, a picture of humility before the Lord.

725
00:41:09,780 --> 00:41:17,360
 And this is probably the biggest barrier

726
00:41:17,360 --> 00:41:21,480
 to your responding to this invitation today, your pride.

727
00:41:21,480 --> 00:41:25,600
 I'll talk about this more in the second service as well,

728
00:41:25,600 --> 00:41:30,600
 but why is it so rare in our worship gatherings

729
00:41:30,600 --> 00:41:37,560
 in the church today for us not all

730
00:41:37,560 --> 00:41:39,320
 to be in this posture right here?

731
00:41:39,320 --> 00:41:45,320
 Why would that be?

732
00:41:46,160 --> 00:41:48,120
 Whoa, that was an unusual Sunday.

733
00:41:48,120 --> 00:41:53,840
 Because all throughout this book,

734
00:41:53,840 --> 00:41:56,480
 when people come before this God,

735
00:41:56,480 --> 00:41:59,580
 it's not just here, it's here.

736
00:41:59,580 --> 00:42:13,360
 So what does it say about us

737
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:18,960
 that we have grown used to coming into gatherings

738
00:42:18,960 --> 00:42:22,680
 before worship for a holy God and never being right here?

739
00:42:22,680 --> 00:42:31,140
 When the Bible clearly invites us to come here.

740
00:42:31,140 --> 00:42:35,760
 Who in this room doesn't need to be there?

741
00:42:35,760 --> 00:42:41,680
 In sin, in suffering, in desperation before God.

742
00:42:45,520 --> 00:42:50,080
 So with this invitation, it's time for the main event.

743
00:42:50,080 --> 00:42:54,320
 As the team joins me out here,

744
00:42:54,320 --> 00:42:58,660
 we're gonna respond to God speaking.

745
00:42:58,660 --> 00:43:02,120
 And I just wanna give you freedom

746
00:43:02,120 --> 00:43:05,080
 to seek God in any number of ways.

747
00:43:05,080 --> 00:43:06,480
 I'm just gonna put these on the screen

748
00:43:06,480 --> 00:43:10,760
 just to get your mind going, but Holy Spirit lead.

749
00:43:10,760 --> 00:43:13,600
 Some of you need to seek God for salvation.

750
00:43:14,920 --> 00:43:18,240
 Some of you need to, I would just ask,

751
00:43:18,240 --> 00:43:21,080
 have you entered into a love relationship,

752
00:43:21,080 --> 00:43:23,360
 intimate communion with God in your life?

753
00:43:23,360 --> 00:43:25,360
 I'm not asking if you've prayed a prayer,

754
00:43:25,360 --> 00:43:27,240
 if you've gone to church or called yourself a Christian.

755
00:43:27,240 --> 00:43:29,520
 I'm asking, do you know God

756
00:43:29,520 --> 00:43:31,740
 in passionate relationship with Him?

757
00:43:31,740 --> 00:43:36,200
 If the answer to that question is,

758
00:43:36,200 --> 00:43:37,560
 no, I've never known God that way,

759
00:43:37,560 --> 00:43:39,520
 or I did at one point, that's a long time ago,

760
00:43:39,520 --> 00:43:42,800
 a lot's happened since then, return to the Lord today.

761
00:43:42,800 --> 00:43:44,960
 He's seeking you right now.

762
00:43:44,960 --> 00:43:50,240
 Seek Him for salvation through confession of sin.

763
00:43:50,240 --> 00:43:53,160
 What sin do you need to confess today?

764
00:43:53,160 --> 00:43:54,840
 Let's examine our hearts and minds.

765
00:43:54,840 --> 00:43:56,000
 Repent of any and all sin.

766
00:43:56,000 --> 00:43:58,600
 Let's not walk out of here holding on to the sin

767
00:43:58,600 --> 00:44:01,560
 we came in here with that He died to free us from.

768
00:44:01,560 --> 00:44:06,000
 Let's seek God through cries for help,

769
00:44:06,000 --> 00:44:07,760
 for yourself, for others.

770
00:44:07,760 --> 00:44:11,520
 How do you, we need God to help us for healing,

771
00:44:11,520 --> 00:44:14,880
 for guidance, for wisdom, for strength, for peace.

772
00:44:14,880 --> 00:44:18,240
 In your life, on others' behalf,

773
00:44:18,240 --> 00:44:20,720
 what a privilege to pray for others.

774
00:44:20,720 --> 00:44:26,720
 Or maybe just to seek God in praise and thanksgiving,

775
00:44:26,720 --> 00:44:29,760
 just spending time praising God for who He is,

776
00:44:29,760 --> 00:44:33,160
 thanking Him for specific things He has done, is doing,

777
00:44:33,160 --> 00:44:36,480
 in your life, around your life, in the world.

778
00:44:36,480 --> 00:44:39,600
 And you might do these things alone,

779
00:44:39,600 --> 00:44:41,840
 or with somebody else, or with a small group.

780
00:44:41,840 --> 00:44:44,680
 So in the next few minutes, just pray however God leads.

781
00:44:44,680 --> 00:44:46,600
 Could be on your own, could be turning to somebody,

